---
import Cmd from "./Cmd.astro";
import flujoClaro from "../assets/flujo-light.svg?raw";
import flujoOscuro from "../assets/flujo-dark.svg?raw";
---
<section class="hero" aria-labelledby="titulo">
  <div class="hero-text">
    <h1 id="titulo">Documentation that doesn't rot.</h1>
    <p class="lede">Your coding agent writes the docs: the README, the architecture and its diagrams, the decisions, the runbooks. DocKeeper ties every sentence and every diagram to the code behind it, and tells you the moment that code changes.</p>
    <div class="hero-actions">
      <Cmd cmd="git clone https://github.com/Nokky21/DocKeeper.git ~/.claude/skills/dockeeper" />
      <a class="textlink" href="#demo">Try it in the browser</a>
    </div>
    <p class="hero-meta">An Agent Skill for Claude Code, Codex, Gemini CLI, Cursor and GitHub Copilot, and a CLI with no dependencies for your CI. Free, local, MIT.</p>
  </div>

  <figure class="window" aria-label="A documentation page written by the agent, its anchors, and the output of dockeeper check">
    <div class="window-bar">
      <span class="dots" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>
      <span class="tabs-doc" aria-hidden="true"><span data-current>ARCHITECTURE.md</span><span>DECISIONS.md</span><span>README.md</span></span>
    </div>
    <div class="window-body">
      <div class="tree" aria-hidden="true">
        <b>docs</b>
        <span data-current>ARCHITECTURE.md</span>
        <span>DECISIONS.md</span>
        <span>PROCEDURES.md</span>
        <span>API.md</span>
        <b>packages/api</b>
        <span>README.md</span>
        <b>packages/web</b>
        <span>README.md</span>
      </div>
      <article class="docpage">
        <span class="tag">#architecture · written by your agent</span>
        <p class="doc-h">Payments</p>
        <p>Every webhook is checked against its signature <span class="claim-hl">before anything is charged</span>. A bad signature stops at a 401 and touches nothing.</p>
        <p class="doc-h2">Flow</p>
        <div class="diagram">
          <div class="light" set:html={flujoClaro} />
          <div class="dark" set:html={flujoOscuro} />
        </div>
        <div class="callout"><b>Warning</b>A charge is never retried after a timeout: the provider is asked for its status first.</div>
      </article>
      <aside class="anchors" aria-label="Anchors on this page">
        <p>Anchors on this page</p>
        <div class="pin"><span>src/webhooks.ts#<wbr>verifySignature</span><span class="v v-OK">OK</span></div>
        <div class="pin"><span>src/payments.ts#<wbr>process</span><span class="v v-OK">OK</span></div>
        <div class="pin"><span>src/payments.ts#<wbr>retryAfterTimeout</span><span class="v v-CHANGED">CHANGED</span></div>
      </aside>
    </div>
    <div class="window-foot"><pre class="term"><span class="c">$ dockeeper check</span>
<span class="ch">CHANGED</span>          docs/ARCHITECTURE.md:14  → src/payments.ts#retryAfterTimeout
                 the content of “retryAfterTimeout” changed (src/payments.ts:40-58)
Summary: 1 CHANGED · 4 OK
  → review the code and the text, then dockeeper fix --aceptar
Result: <span class="ch">FAIL</span></pre></div>
  </figure>
</section>
